<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Solsonès</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Solsonès is a comarca, or county, in the pre-Pyrenean interior of Catalonia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, with its capital at Solsona, a cathedral city and seat of a bishopric. Largely rural and wooded, it is one of the most thinly populated comarques, living from farming, forestry and tourism. In antiquity it formed part of the lands of the Iberian Lacetani.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/solsones.jpg" alt="Solsonès" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Catalan Heralder · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solson%C3%A8s_(Catalunya).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
